BB's IRISH TRADITIONAL TUNE LIBRARY\
Dance Tunes from "The ROCHE COLLECTION OF TRADITIONAL IRISH MUSIC" \
Dublin 1927; reprint Cork 1984\
Volume 3\
= = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = =\
\
Transcriber's note:\
[1] Many of the reels in the Roche volumes that are single (8/8) \
may not be played that way today. I have kept most of them as they\
appeared in the book, but feel free to change them at your \
discretion.\
[2] Similarly, many of the tunes that are D minor in the book may\
be better considered as D modal (thus avoiding problems with F\
naturals). Some of the tunes I know to be D modal I have changed;\
others not familiar to me I have left as D minor. \
[3] Some of Roche's titles are suspect if we use O'Neill as the\
standard. For example, Roche's "Mills Are Grinding" and "Humors\
of Cappa" share only the names with O'Neill. In other instances\
familiar names are given to unfamiliar tunes (e.g. "Heather Breeze");\
conversely, unfamiliar names are applied to familiar tunes (e.g.\
"Bundle and Go" for "Larry O Gaff"). Then there's "Sweet Biddy\
Daly" which the Roches seem to think is "Saddle the Pony".\
\
Suffice it to say that these volumes keep life interesting for \
an archivist!\
\
= = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = =\
\
This volume contains a fair number of marches, set dances and \
quadrilles.\
\
Where the marches and set dances could be made into useful dance \
tunes, I have taken the liberty of doing so. \
\
The quadrilles - which consist of nameless tunes - seem to be of \
interest mainly to a student of Irish dance history, so I have kept \
them in this file for research purposes only. \
\
Any material that will not be included in the Library will be\
found in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.capeirish.com/ittl/tunefolders/53/533/533-omitted.txt"}}{\fldrslt separate folder}}.\
\
= = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = =\
\
Also in this volume are Roche's "Old Set Tunes". They are musically \
valuable so I have given them names and treated them like any other \
dance tune in the book.\
\
= = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = =\
